{"shortDescription":"Asia fuel oil markets were mixed on Monday, with very low sulphur fuel oil (VLSFO) easing while high sulphur fuel oil (HSFO) maintained support.Spot VLSFO traded at a softer premium compared to last session's value, while offers dropped for later September dates.The market is still expected to reta…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Asia fuel oil markets were mixed on Monday, with very low sulphur fuel oil (VLSFO) easing while high sulphur fuel oil (HSFO) maintained support."]},{"type":"p","children":["Spot VLSFO traded at a softer premium compared to last session's value, while offers dropped for later September dates."]},{"type":"p","children":["The market is still expected to retain a floor as refiners have lowered fuel oil production while prioritising the output of diesel and other products that command higher margins."]},{"type":"p","children":["HSFO continued to hold firm on limited prompt supply. The product traded at a higher cash premium on Monday, while bids edged higher into October."]},{"type":"p","children":["Some activity for spot tenders was underway for September loadings and deliveries, according to market sources."]},{"type":"p","children":["Indonesia's Pertamina offered 200,000 barrels of low-sulphur waxy residue for loading between September 17 and 18, in a tender that closed on Monday."]},{"type":"p","children":["Meanwhile, Vietnam's Nghi Son is seeking 30,000 to 35,000 tons of straight-run fuel oil for delivery between September 23 and 28. The tender will close on Tuesday, according to a notice on its website."]},{"type":"p","children":["OTHER NEWS"]},{"type":"p","children":["- Oil prices were near six-week highs on Monday as tit-for-tat strikes between the U.S. and Iran on vessels sailing in the Strait of Hormuz and other areas kept crude oil flows in the Middle East low."]},{"type":"p","children":["- OPEC+ kept ​its oil output policy unchanged for October at a meeting on Sunday, it said in a statement, as the producer group needs to agree new quotas before deciding its next output steps."]},{"type":"p","children":["- An average of 10 commodity ships transited the Strait of Hormuz per day over the past 10 days, the lowest since May, according to shipping data on Monday, after U.S. and Iranian strikes on tankers."]},{"type":"p","children":["- Nigeria's Dangote Group will sign documents for the initial public offering of its refinery business with advisers and others involved in Africa's biggest-ever share sale at a ceremony starting around 1100 GMT on Monday, the company said."]},{"type":"p","children":["WINDOW TRADES"]},{"type":"p","children":["- 180-cst HSFO: No trade."]},{"type":"p","children":["- 380-cst HSFO: Two trades."]},{"type":"p","children":["- 0.5% VLSFO: One trade."]},{"type":"p","children":["ASSESSMENTS"]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["FUEL OIL"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["CASH ($/T)"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["ASIA CLOSE"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["RIC"]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Cargo - 180cst"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["594.55"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["(FO180-SIN)"]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Diff - 180cst"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["24.17"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["(FO180-SIN-DIF)"]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","chi